{"id":"u-e201b45a-308b-4df1-b892-2a3e720bb08b","src":"community","title":"Rise of the Valkyrie","author":"JUD STEELE","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/TnktkL-rise-of-the-valkyrie","desc":"Inspired by Norse Valkyries and Spartan training principles, the programme uses 300-rep workouts to develop strength, endurance, mental toughness, and physical confidence in a single session.\n\nThis is training with intent, not aesthetics alone.\n\nWhy 300-rep Spartan workouts?\n\n300-rep training:\n-Builds full-body strength and muscular endurance\n-Forces mental resilience under fatigue\n-Creates a strong, athletic physique without chasing isolation\n-Trains the body to keep moving under pressure\n\nThis style mirrors:\n-Battlefield conditioning\n-Combat readiness\n-Real-world physical demand\n\nYou don’t stop because you’re tired — you adapt and continue.\n\nWhy it’s specifically powerful for women:\nThe Valkyrie Programme recognises that women:\n-Excel at endurance and repeat-effort output\n-Respond well to high-volume, moderate-load training\n-Build lean muscle without excessive bulk\n-Thrive when training has meaning and identity\n\nThis isn’t about shrinking, burning, or “toning” — It’s about earning strength and reducing fear of effort.\n\nWhat it develops physically:\n✔ Strong legs and glutes\n✔ Dense, athletic shoulders and back\n✔ Powerful core and posture\n✔ Grip strength and resilience\n✔ Work capacity and stamina\n\nThe result is a body that looks capable, grounded, and powerful.\n\nWhat it develops mentally:\nThe real goal of Valkyrie training is psychological strength:\n-Confidence under fatigue\n-Calm when breathing is heavy\n-Pride in completing difficult tasks\n-A shift from “Can I?” to “I will.”\n\nCompleting a 300-rep workout becomes a rite of passage.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Athletics","Women's","Bodyweight Fitness","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":30,"joins":3,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-09-26T07:01:57.280Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":25}]},{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":50}]},{"n":"Push Up","sets":[{"r":50}]},{"n":"Lunge (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":50}]},{"n":"Abs Crunch (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":50}]},{"n":"Kettlebell Clean and Press","sets":[{"r":50}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":25}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Goblet Squat","sets":[{"r":60}]},{"n":"Kettlebell Clean and Press","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Renegade Row","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Push Up (Incline)","sets":[{"r":60}]},{"n":"Reverse Lunge (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":50}]},{"n":"Decline Sit Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":50}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"r":60}]},{"n":"Hip Thrust (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":50}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Machine)","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Cable)","sets":[{"r":30}]},{"n":"Tricep Rope Push Down (Cable)","sets":[{"r":30}]},{"n":"Abs Crunch (Machine)","sets":[{"r":30}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":50}]},{"n":"Dumbbell Thruster","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Single Arm Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":50}]},{"n":"Push Up","sets":[{"r":60}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Machine)","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Sit Up","sets":[{"r":60}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":50}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":50}]},{"n":"Front Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":50}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":60}]},{"n":"Russian Twist (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":50}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":60}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Machine)","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Machine)","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"r":40}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Cable)","sets":[{"r":30}]},{"n":"Tricep Rope Push Do